                </div>
                <h1 class="content-title">UI Anatomy: <span class="gradient-text">Forms, Lists &amp; The Filter Engine</span></h1>
                <p class="content-subtitle">
                    Master how humans interact with data in ServiceNow — list view controls, the breadcrumb query engine, 
                    form section anatomy, related lists, and visual form design.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Section 1: Dual UI Principle -->
            <section class="content-section" id="dual-ui">
                <h2>The Dual UI Principle: Lists vs. Forms</h2>
                <p>
                    Every table in ServiceNow is experienced through two complementary interface modes:
                </p>

                <div class="feature-grid">
                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>The List View (Macro Perspective)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            A high-density tabular view displaying multiple records at once. Designed for triage, searching, 
                            sorting, filtering, and bulk-updating hundreds of work items simultaneously.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>The Form View (Micro Perspective)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            A detailed single-record document view. Designed for data entry, step-by-step diagnostic workflows, 
                            journal work note updates, and executing action buttons (*Resolve, Approve, Rollback*).
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 2: List View Anatomy -->
            <section class="content-section" id="list-anatomy">
                <h2>List View Anatomy &amp; Power Controls</h2>
                <p>
                    The List view is packed with built-in productivity tools:
                </p>

                <div class="feature-grid">
                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>1. Column Header Sorting &amp; Grouping</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Click any column header to sort ascending/descending. Right-click any column header and select 
                            <strong>Group By [Field]</strong> to instantly collapse records into visual accordion buckets 
                            (e.g., group 500 incidents by *Assignment Group*).
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>2. Personalize List Columns (Gear Icon ⚙️)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Clicking the gear icon in the top-left of a list lets individual users add, remove, or reorder columns 
                            on their screen without changing the view for other team members.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>3. List Cell Inline Editing</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Double-click any editable cell (like <em>State</em> or <em>Assigned To</em>) to update the record directly 
                            from the grid without loading the full form page.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>4. Natural Language Column Search</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Type in the column search bar using wildcard syntax:
                            <br>• <code>*vpn</code> $\rightarrow$ searches text containing "vpn" anywhere in the field.
                            <br>• <code>!vpn</code> $\rightarrow$ excludes records containing "vpn".
                            <br>• <code>=prdsrv</code> $\rightarrow$ exact match.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 3: The Filter Engine -->
            <section class="content-section" id="filter-engine">
                <h2>The Breadcrumb Filter Engine (Querying like a Pro)</h2>
                <p>
                    Clicking the funnel icon (🔍) at the top of any list opens the <strong>Condition Builder</strong>. 
                    Queries are assembled using a simple 3-part syntax:
                </p>

                <div class="code-block">
                    <div class="code-header">
                        <span class="code-lang">Filter Condition Structure</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="code-body">
<pre><code>[ Field ]  --  [ Operator ]  --  [ Value ]
Example: [ Active ] [ is ] [ true ]  AND  [ Priority ] [ is ] [ 1 - Critical ]</code></pre>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="tabs-container">
                    <div class="tabs-header">
                        <button class="tab-btn active" data-tab="tab-operators">Common Operators</button>
                        <button class="tab-btn" data-tab="tab-breadcrumbs">Breadcrumb Navigation</button>
                        <button class="tab-btn" data-tab="tab-copy-query">Copy Encoded Query</button>
                    </div>

                    <div class="tab-panel active" id="tab-operators">
                        <h3>Core Filter Operators</h3>
                        <table class="data-table">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Operator</th>
                                    <th>Data Type Supported</th>
                                    <th>Operational Meaning</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>is / is not</code></td>
                                    <td>String, Choice, Reference</td>
                                    <td>Exact value equality check.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>contains / does not contain</code></td>
                                    <td>String, HTML</td>
                                    <td>Wildcard substring search anywhere inside the text.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>is one of</code></td>
                                    <td>Choice, Reference</td>
                                    <td>Matches any selected values from a multi-select list (SQL <code>IN (...)</code>).</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>is empty / is not empty</code></td>
                                    <td>All Data Types</td>
                                    <td>Checks for <code>NULL</code> or unpopulated fields.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>on / between / dynamic</code></td>
                                    <td>Date / DateTime</td>
                                    <td>Evaluates time windows (e.g. *Created on "Today"*, *Opened "This Quarter"*).</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>

                    <div class="tab-panel" id="tab-breadcrumbs">
                        <h3>Breadcrumb Trail Navigation</h3>
                        <p>
                            As you apply filters, ServiceNow generates an interactive breadcrumb trail at the top of the screen:
                            <br><code>All &gt; Active = true &gt; Priority = 1 - Critical &gt; State != Resolved</code>
                        </p>
                        <ul class="feature-bullet-list">
                            <li>Clicking any segment in the breadcrumb immediately filters the list up to that exact step.</li>
                            <li>Right-clicking a value in a list cell and selecting <strong>Show Matching</strong> or <strong>Filter Out</strong> adds to the breadcrumb instantly.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="tab-panel" id="tab-copy-query">
                        <h3>Developer Superpower: Copy Encoded Query</h3>
                        <p>
                            Right-clicking the last item in the breadcrumb trail and selecting <strong>Copy Query</strong> 
                            copies the platform's raw encoded query string (e.g. <code>active=true^priority=1^state!=6</code>).
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Developers paste this string directly into JavaScript server scripts via <code>gr.addEncodedQuery(...)</code>, 
                            eliminating the need to hand-code complex SQL queries!
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 4: Form Anatomy -->
            <section class="content-section" id="form-anatomy">
                <h2>Form View Anatomy &amp; Related Lists</h2>
                <p>
                    When you click into a record, the Form View organizes fields into logical operational zones:
                </p>

                <div class="diagram-block">
                    <div class="diagram-title">Visual Architecture of a ServiceNow Form</div>
                    <div class="mermaid">
                    graph TD
                        HDR["1. Form Header: Back Button, Number, Attachment Clip, UI Actions (Save/Submit)"]
                        
                        HDR --> SEC1["2. Primary Section (2-Column Split): Caller, Category, CI, Priority, State"]
                        SEC1 --> SEC2["3. Tabbed Sections: Resolution Details, Notes (Work Notes / Comments), SLAs"]
                        SEC2 --> REL["4. Related Lists (Sub-Tables at Bottom): Child Incidents, Incident Tasks, Approvers"]
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-grid">
                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Activity Stream (Journal Log)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Combines **Customer Visible Comments** (yellow border, seen by the end user on the portal) 
                            and **Internal Work Notes** (yellow background, visible only to ITIL agents) into a single timestamped audit timeline.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Related Lists (Bottom Grids)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Displays child tables linked to this record via foreign keys (e.g. all 3 <code>task_sla</code> timers 
                            counting down on this incident, or all <code>change_task</code> records assigned for a server upgrade).
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 5: Form Layout vs Form Design -->
            <section class="content-section" id="form-customization">
                <h2>Form Layout vs. Form Design (How Admins Customize Forms)</h2>
                <p>
                    ServiceNow provides two built-in configuration tools to modify form layouts:
                </p>

                <table class="data-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Feature Dimension</th>
                            <th>Form Layout (Classic Slushbucket)</th>
                            <th>Form Design (Modern Drag-and-Drop)</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Interface</strong></td>
                            <td>Dual-list box (Slushbucket: Available Columns $\rightarrow$ Selected Columns).</td>
                            <td>Visual canvas with drag-and-drop field palette.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Best Used For</strong></td>
                            <td>Quickly adding existing fields to a section or configuring Related Lists.</td>
                            <td>Arranging 2-column grids, creating new fields on the fly, and organizing multi-tab sections.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>How to Access</strong></td>
                            <td>Form Header Menu $\rightarrow$ <em>Configure</em> $\rightarrow$ <em>Form Layout</em>.</td>
                            <td>Form Header Menu $\rightarrow$ <em>Configure</em> $\rightarrow$ <em>Form Design</em>.</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </section>

